    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present No. 47 Pier 19, a superb two-bedroom, ground floor apartment presented in excellent condition throughout, ideally positioned within this popular and well-maintained development. Boasting a C BER rating, this bright and spacious home is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, investors, and those looking to downsize alike.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a spacious open-plan living and dining area, a well-appointed fully fitted kitchen, two generous double bedrooms, and a recently upgraded, fully tiled family bathroom, finished to a high standard. The property benefits from electric heating throughout and enjoys an abundance of natural light.\n\nFurther enhancing the appeal of this attractive apartment is its private courtyard, providing a secluded outdoor space. This versatile outdoor area offers a peaceful extension of the living accommodation, creating an ideal setting to unwind while adding both charm and practicality to the property. \n\nAdding to its appeal, the property is offered to the market with no onward chain, allowing for a straightforward purchase process.\n\nPier 19 enjoys an enviable location within walking distance of many of Dublin's most notable landmarks, including St. James's Hospital, the Guinness Storehouse, Dublin Castle, and Christ Church Cathedral. Prospective investors will appreciate its close proximity to Trinity College Dublin, the Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland, and Griffith College Dublin. A wealth of cafés, restaurants, and bars are on the doorstep, while Vicar Street offers an excellent programme of live entertainment. The area is exceptionally well served by public transport, with regular bus routes and the Luas nearby, while Dublin Bikes stations at Christchurch, Francis Street, and John Street West provide convenient access throughout the city.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
